title: 'statement-store: rerun expiry sweep while a backlog remains'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The statement store's background task removed at most 10,000 expired statements every 31
    seconds, which capped expiry throughput at roughly 320 statements per second. Under sustained
    load the backlog of expired statements grew until the store filled up and rejected new
    statements with `StoreFull`.

    `Store::enforce_limits` now returns `true` when expired statements are still due after its
    bounded pass, and the background task then runs the next pass immediately instead of waiting
    for the next 31 second tick. Each pass stays bounded, so the lock is still released between
    passes. Each rerun also runs the per-account allowance phase, which costs more on a store
    with many accounts.
crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: patch
